      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Under the Consumer Act, any seller or manufacturer that gives an express warranty must put the warranty terms in clear, understandable written language, identify the warrantor, name the party covered, specify the products or parts covered, explain what will be done if a defect occurs and at whose expense, tell the consumer what to do to claim the warranty, and set the period for performance.  The buyer only needs to show the warranty card or official receipt to enforce the warranty; no other documents may be demanded.  Any agreement that tries to waive the written‑warranty requirement is void.",
