      "text": "A consumer may file a petition or a letter‑complaint with the Department of Trade and Industry, which may then commence an investigation. The consumer arbitration officer conducts a hearing, giving the parties notice of the date, time and place and attaching a copy of the complaint. The officer first seeks a settlement; if none is reached, the officer may formally investigate, hear evidence and decide the case. The decision must be rendered within fifteen (15) days after the investigation ends.",
